          "type": "text",
          "content": "单项选择。\n(   )1. It’s such an interesting story ________ everybody likes it.\nA. as               B. that          C. so that         D. which\n(   )2. I don’t like him. I’d rather ________ in than ________ to play with him.\nA. to play, to go      B. stay, go       C. to play, go      D. stay, to go\n(   )3. He is very old, ________ he still works very hard.\nA. if               B. when         C. and            D. but\n(   )4. Mrs. Smith likes music ________ her husband likes sport.\nA. while            B. or            C. for            D. so\n(   )5. ________ Tom ________ Mary is free. You’d better play with others.\nA. Both, and        B. Not only, but also   C. Neither, nor   D. Either, or\n(   )6. They didn’t start to work ________ the boss arrived.\nA. so              B. as soon as         C. while        D. until\n(   )7. ________ you’re all here, we can work out a solution.\nA. Because         B. Though           C. Since        D For\n(   )8. The child is clever ________ healthy.\nA. as soon as        B. as good as        C. as well as     D. as tall as\n(   )9. We must set off now, ________ we’ll miss the last train.\nA. and             B. while            C. then          D. or\n(   )10. Can you name three countries ________ Chinese is used as one of their languages?\nA. that             B. which            C. where        D. there\n(   )11. We were getting ready to go out ______ it began to rain.\nA. where            B. when           C. since            D. if\n(   )12. We love spring ______ there’re beautiful flowers everywhere.\nA. but              B. if              C. though           D. because\n(   )13. The work was _______ difficult _______ it took us quite a long time to do it.\nA. such, that         B. so, that         C. too, that          D. too, to\n(   )14. I’ll tell him to give you a call ______ he comes back.\nA. because          B. since           C. as soon as         D. but\n(   )15. -- Why did Li Lei use a pencil?    -- _______ his pen was broken.\nA. Because         B. When           C. Until             D. If\n(   )16. I think Chinese is more popular ______ any other subject.\nA. than            B. for              C. as               D. then\n(   )17. What do I have to do ______ I want to be thinner?\nA. if              B. because          C. since             D. for\n(   )18. I won’t turn off the light ______ you’ve finished reading.\nA. when           B. after           C. as soon as         D. until\n(   )19. I’ll study English and other objects _______ I can.\nA. so hard as        B. as hard as       C. so hardly as       D. as hardly as\n(   )20. Though it rained heavily, _______ were still playing on the playground.\nA. they            B. so they          C. but they          D. and they\n(   )21. You should finish your exercises ______ you go to bed.\nA. after            B. before           C. because         D. if\n(   )22. -- Are we going to West Hill Farm by bike?\n-- No. By bus, _______ it is quite far from here.\nA. if              B. when            C. though          D. because\n(   )23. Mr. Read has taught in that small town ______ he left Canada in 1988.\nA. when           B. after             C. for             D. since\n(   )24. I’m ______ busy getting ready for Christmas _______ I have no time to write to you.\nA. not, until        B. too, to            C. so, that         D. neither, nor\n(   )25. You’ll do better in English ______ you work harder.\nA. or             B. than              C. if              D. before\n(   )26. Tom didn’t go to school yesterday ______ he was ill.\nA. but            B. until              C. if              D. because\n(   )27. Li Hua ______ in the factory since she left school ten years ago.\nA. works        B. worked         C. has worked    D. had worked\n(   )28. -- I’m going to Hangzhou for a holiday this weekend.\n-- ________ you are there, can you buy me some green tea?\nA. Because       B. If                 C. While           D. After\n(   )29. What shall we do ______ it rains tomorrow?\nA. so            B. if                 C. but             D. because\n(   )30. If you ______ him tomorrow, please ask him if he _______ to work on the farm with us.\nA. see, goes       B. will see, goes       C. will see, will go   D. see, will go\n(   )31. The room is ______ dirty ______ we don’t want to stay here.\nA. so, that        B. such, that           C. either, or         D. as, as\n(   )32. _______ he’s very young, _______ he knows several languages.\nA. Though, but    B. Because, so          C. Though, /       D. Because, /\n(   )33. They will have a sports meeting if it ______ tomorrow.\nA. won’t rain     B. will rain             C. doesn’t rain     D. rains\n(   )34. My parents will go out for an outing with me if they ______ free next Sunday.\nA. will be        B. are                 C. have           D. will have\n(   )35. We ______ Xiao Li since she was a little girl.\nA. know         B. had known           C. have known     D. knew\n(   )36. Could you ring me up as soon as he ______?\nA. arrived        B. would arrive         C. arrives          D. will arrive\n(   )37. We ______ TV when the telephone ________.\nA. watched, was ringing                   B. were watching, rang\nC. watch, rings                          D. are watching, rang\n(   )38. Kate ______ to bed until her father returned yesterday evening.\nA. won’t go        B. doesn’t go           C. went           D. didn’t go\n(   )39. If the child _______, please telephone the police.\nA. found          B. is found            C. was found         D. has found\n(   )40. If you ______ here tomorrow, I’ll be delighted.\nA. comes          B. will come          C. came             D. come\n参考答案\n1. B 2. D 3. D 4. A 5. C\n6. D 7. C 8. C 9. D 10. C\n11-15ACCDA\n16-20BBBDB\n21-25BDDCC\n26-30DCCBD\n31-35ACCBC\n36-40CBDBD"
